{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2183","id":4939893410,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAivEQM8AAAABJnDKog","html_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2183","diff_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2183.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2183.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/issues/2183","number":2183,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: add nine-key Pinyin input with syllable selection","user":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Add Chinese nine-key Pinyin using the existing `luna_pinyin` dictionary and user dictionary. Enable `luna_pinyin_t9` through the existing scheme selector; both stock themes provide the layout.\n\nSupport syllable selection/locking, focus changes, unlock, undo, cancel, literal digits/symbols and editor-boundary reset. Native revisions reject stale spelling actions. Responses keep one bounded spelling snapshot alongside the existing batched candidate response. Related #1464, #1299 and #459.\n\n**Draft: the maintainer-requested physical-device verification remains NOT RUN.**\n\nHead `8a1ee0ea` is rebased onto upstream `a047f747`, with four linear Conventional Commits. The obsolete local #2187 candidate change was dropped in favor of the version merged upstream. Included Unicode and deferred-view dependencies match the reviewed #2186 and #2188 changes. The scheme-restoration and editor-required ASCII fixes remain. Fork release/Pages configuration, prediction, privacy policy and candidate pinning remain outside this PR.\n\nValidation for this source:\n\n- [Upstream CI](https://github.com/osfans/trime/actions/runs/40527129836): all five jobs succeeded, including unit-test and Lint tasks. The workflow did not export a precise application test count.\n- Fresh host checks passed 743 T9 assertions, 115 Unicode CheckJNI assertions and 46 UTF-16 offset assertions. The recorded host librime engine was reused; the current T9 test programs were rebuilt.\n- Original four-ABI Debug APKs were audited without modification or re-signing. Their actual producer is merge `0ef0eb55`, whose complete Git tree equals head `8a1ee0ea`; build metadata and APK bytes are not claimed to be direct-head builds.\n- The same original x86_64 Debug APK completed the targeted 12 sessions/14 logical checks on Android 5.0 and Android 15 r2, with 134 captures and 110 strict editor-text pairs per system. Both VMs shut down normally; the Android 15 log collector returned 255 on ADB disconnect, a retained capture limitation. The earlier API35 attempt had system startup ANRs and two low-watermark kills before Trime startup; that failed attempt remains recorded.\n\nDependency/tool, Debug-signature and runtime diagnostics remain documented; no zero-warning, Release, performance or physical-device acceptance is claimed. The 44 physical-device result fields remain NOT_RUN, so this PR stays Draft.\n\n[Input behavior and switching contract](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/blob/8a1ee0ea6538e220fcddf31ed6fd491f5bc3cca7/doc/t9-input.md).\n\n[Current validation scope and retained evidence](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/blob/d31d91830653e946bc0b1